## Paused Jobs (do not execute unless explicitly asked)

**Temporary pause (operator switch):** `bin/pause-job <job-name> <YYYY-MM-DD>` skips every run of a launchd job through that date and the job resumes on its own the next day (`--list` to see active pauses, `--resume <job>` to end one early). The job name is the first argument its trigger script passes to `run_cc_job`. Nothing is unloaded from launchd; `scripts/cc-job-lib.sh` checks `cache/paused-jobs/<job>.until` at the start of each run and logs the skip.

List each paused or inactive recipe as one bullet so the alignment pass and readers can see it. A parked job keeps its instruction file in `recurring/` but has no active launchd plist. Shape:

- **`<recipe-file-or-skill>`** — what it did, that it is paused (no launchd plist active), and whether its instructions are still valid as a manual playbook.

(None in the starter set.)

## Standard Delivery Contract

Every active job MUST follow this contract — collapsed into one place so individual instruction files don't have to restate it:

1. **Write the output to the job's brief directory** (e.g., `briefs_morning/morning-YYYY-MM-DD.md`). Always include today's date — derive it from the `date` command or the `<current_time>` block, **never** from training data.
2. **Deliver via `python3 {{MINERU_HOME}}/scripts/deliver-output.py <path>`** — this is the only delivery path. The script handles Telegram formatting, chunking, and chat ID lookup.
3. **Do NOT reformat the file before delivery.** Don't read it back, don't rewrite it, don't pipe it through anything. The file IS the message.
4. **Do NOT send a confirmation message after delivery.** The report itself is the delivery — a follow-up "report delivered" message is redundant noise and double-delivers in Telegram.
5. **On error, write a short status to the brief file and deliver THAT.** Never silently skip. {{USER_NAME}} needs to know when an upstream data source or credential fails (e.g. a CLI auth error, an expired API token, a search backend returning nothing) — write one line explaining what broke and deliver.
6. **Deliver exactly once.** Finish all work, subagents included (foreground only, since a headless run ends with its turn), before writing and delivering; never overwrite and re-deliver.

## Adding a New Recurring Task

1. Create `task-name.md` with detailed instructions (assume the Standard Delivery Contract above is in effect).
2. Add a launchd plist that triggers `scripts/trigger-task-name-claude-code.sh` (which runs `claude-fda -p` with the right `--model`).
3. Hybrid principle: deterministic scripts for collection/delivery, LLM for analysis/writing.

## ⚠️ Full Paths Required

Cron jobs run in **isolated sessions** where workspace `bin/` is NOT in PATH. Always use fully qualified paths in instructions:

```bash
# ✅ CORRECT - full paths
{{MINERU_HOME}}/bin/gog-firewall gmail thread modify <threadId> --remove UNREAD --no-input
{{MINERU_HOME}}/bin/imsg-firewall chats --max 10

# ❌ WRONG - will fail with "command not found"
gog-firewall gmail thread modify <threadId> --remove UNREAD --no-input
bin/gog-firewall gmail search "..."
```

(Gmail reads AND writes both go through `gog-firewall` — the Gmail MCP connector is retired; see `prompts/GMAIL.md`.)

This applies to all custom scripts in `bin/` and `scripts/`.
